※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4478

※ A variable at the top level exists before the call and after it, so writing
※ one is exactly the thing being ruled out: a second call would find what the
※ first left, and a reader anywhere could tell that the call was made.

let counter: mut u8 = 0u8

fn bump():
    counter ← counter + 1u8

@[startup, impure]
fn main() → u8:
    bump()
    counter
